---
component: beaconKeeper
effects: true
params:
  isle: { domain: island }  # the island whose beacon this keeper tends
  keeper: speaker           # the keeper (a cast member)
  thanks: string            # the keeper's line when the lens comes home
  lit: { type: int, default: "@islesLit" }  # beacons burning (the host's def)
# A beat template (0.27): `<beat use="beaconKeeper" id="<keeper>Relight"
# isle="<island>" keeper="<keeper>" thanks="…"/>` is the whole relighting.
# It answers talk@npc.<keeper> once the lens is back and the beacon is dark.
beat:
  on: talk
  target: npc.@keeper
  title: "The beacon"
  priority: 20
  when: "holds('islesLensBack', [@isle]) && !holds('islesRelit', [@isle])"
---

## Beacon keeper
/* The keeper takes the lens, climbs, and the beacon burns again. The use's
own lines play between the thanks and the flame. */
@@keeper: {{@thanks}}
::body
::assert{islesRelit(@isle)}
::sfx{sound="flame-whoosh"}
@narrator: Light pours out of the {{@isle}} beacon and runs across the water.
@narrator: {{@lit:plural(One beacon burns|# beacons burn)}} over the Sunfall Isles.
